  "text": "The mother of someone's mother or father.\n\nRested with the body supported on a seat.\n\nThe final boat or event in this sequence.\n\nDifferent from the one already mentioned.\n\nThe empty seed boat bobs at its mooring.\n\nA unit of language that carries meaning.\n\nDiscover or work out where something is.\n\nA narrow mark or a row of written words.\n\nA bridge made for people to walk across.\n\nM-24 1q-1-20 24-20t24 20q-1 8-24 8T-24 1\n\nOne side or sheet of a piece of writing.\n\nOffered an idea for someone to consider.\n\nPlaced something or started an activity.\n\nKeep the bridge pieces beside the river.\n\nStory paused. Resume when you are ready.\n\nThe dock worker who wrote The Torn Wing.\n\nStop for a while, intending to continue.\n\nMore suitable or successful than before.\n\nMoved into a curved or lowered position.\n\nOn a surface, or moving to that surface.\n\nThe seed is planted in Grandma’s garden.\n\nM-50-9h13m74 0h13M-31-52l8 11m44-11-8 11\n\nAll four parts of the ending you played.\n\nDescribes a possible or expected action.\n\nPay attention to sounds or spoken words.\n\nM19 4C8 2 3 8 5 15s14 3 14-11ZM5 19 15 9\n\nPut another thing in place of something.\n\nAt the usual time · Mara tells her story\n\nTaking care to avoid mistakes or damage.\n\nAgreement that someone may do something.\n\nFelt that someone or something mattered.\n\nThe crossing is ready. Guide Pip across.\n\nA large natural stream of flowing water.\n\nTake food into the mouth and swallow it.\n\nReading help for these words and choices\n\nAll of something, from beginning to end.\n\nImages showing people, places or events.\n\nShows where someone or something starts.\n\nLet someone see or understand something.\n\nAble to keep water from passing through.\n\nPip and Grandma plant the seed together.\n\nThought something was likely to happen.",
